<p>I went out to <a href="http://briercrest.ca/chs">Caronport High School</a> for Grade 12 to see if/where my skills at hockey would take me. They took me to the first try-out where I was promptly cut. After <a href="http://briercrest.ca/college">four years of Bible School</a> I graduated with a BA in Sports Ministry. So how did I end up leading a team of 20+ people in a <a href="https://thelifeproject.com">99.9% online ministry</a>?</p>
<p><strong>I read a lot. I research a lot. I build things.</strong></p>
<p>This page is a list of the things I turn to when I need to figure out how to make something happen.</p>
<p><strong>Laravel:</strong> <a href="http://laracasts.com">Laracasts</a> (Courses) | <a href="https://adamwathan.me/test-driven-laravel/">Test Driven Laravel</a> (Course) | <a href="https://mattstauffer.co/laravel-up-and-running">Laravel Up and Running</a> (Book) | <a href="https://larachat.co">Larachat</a> (Slack) | <a href="http://laravel.com/docs">Documentation</a></p>
<p><strong>Statamic:</strong> <a href="http://statamic.slack.com">Statamic Community</a> (Slack) | <a href="http://learnstatamic.com">Learn Statamic</a> (Course) | <a href="http://docs.statamic.com">Documentation</a></p>
<p><strong>Vue:</strong> <a href="http://vuecasts.com">Vuecasts</a> (Courses) | <a href="https://leanpub.com/vuejs2">Majesty of Vue.js 2</a> (Book)</p>
<p><strong>Git:</strong> <a href="https://vuejs.org/v2/guide/">Guide</a> | <a href="http://gettinggit.com">Getting Git</a> (Course) | <a href="https://git-scm.com/book/">Pro Git</a> (Book)</p>
<p>When all else fails (but sometimes first) I go to <a href="http://google.com">Google</a> which will usually send me to <a href="http://stackoverflow.com">Stack Overflow</a>.</p>
